 "oracle": "REQ-M5-010 services.md v1.7, v1.8, v1.9: the manager watchdogs Ready services (watchdog=<ticks>, PING/PONG on the boot channel). `hung` (watchdog=50, role hang) answers READY then stops servicing, so a missed PONG period has it force-killed (EXIT_KILLED=131072); with max_restarts=1 it is restarted once, hangs again and is given up (given_up, restarts=1). `pong` (watchdog=50, role ready, its manifest line with two spaces before the arg — v1.8 trims them) answers every PING and stays ready (restarts=0); each PONG is traced (`svc|pong`, at least 3). `closer` (watchdog=50) closes its boot channel after READY: it can no longer be asked, so it is killed as hung (failed, 131072). `early` (timeout 50) hangs before READY without reading its channel: failed at the timeout, still alive 200 ticks after its start (the grace runs from the timeout), then forced (failed, 131072). `stubborn` (no watchdog, role hang) ignores STOP: 150 ticks after the STOP it is still stopping, then the grace ends in process_kill (stopped, 131072). `loud` first sends 100 bytes on its boot channel, more than any request (v1.9: discarded and answered ERR BAD_REQUEST), then READY: it is ready (restarts=0). The manager keeps answering LIST; no frame leak; exit 33",
